# Review routing. The point is not gatekeeping -- it's that the parts of Bridge where a
# mistake destroys a translation team's work always get a second reader, while the parts
# where a mistake is visible and cheap can move quickly.
#
# CODEOWNERS only does anything once branch protection on `main` has "Require review
# from Code Owners" enabled. Until then this file is documentation.
#
# Last matching pattern wins, so the faster-lane entries are deliberately at the bottom.

# Default: anything not matched below.
*                                       @RevantCI

# --- Needs maintainer review, always -----------------------------------------

# The analysis engine: Stages 5-9, the QA adapters, and the vendored Greek Room trees.
/engine/                                @RevantCI

# The Tauri/Rust shell, including sidecar lifecycle and the passage-semantic wire.
/src-tauri/                             @RevantCI

# Companion-database schema and migrations. A bad migration is unrecoverable for a real
# project. Note there is no migrations/ directory and no .sql files: the whole schema
# and every _MIGRATION_V1..V14 block live inside this one module.
/engine/tc_ai_bridge/passage_semantic_repository.py   @RevantCI
/engine/tc_ai_bridge/passage_semantic_models.py       @RevantCI

# The JSON wire schema and its fixtures.
/schemas/                               @RevantCI

# Golden files. Changes here also need the goldens:rebaselined label (see ci.yml).
# They are not in a goldens/ directory -- they sit beside the tests that read them.
/engine/tests/fixtures/                 @RevantCI

# Release and CI machinery.
/.github/                               @RevantCI

# Fixture-seeding and build scripts. The engine suite imports three of these directly,
# so a change here can break tests without touching engine/.
/scripts/                               @RevantCI

# The documents that define how we work and what the constraints are.
/CLAUDE.md                              @RevantCI
/CONTRIBUTING.md                        @RevantCI
/docs/HANDOFF.md                        @RevantCI
/docs/BUILD_LOG.md                      @RevantCI
/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md                   @RevantCI
/docs/DECISIONS.md                      @RevantCI
/docs/QA_TEST_MATRIX.md                 @RevantCI

# --- Faster lane --------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend work: still reviewed, but either of us can approve it.
#
# TODO(maintainer): replace @HANDLE-TBD with the real GitHub username before enabling
# "Require review from Code Owners". GitHub silently ignores an unknown handle -- the
# rule does not error, it just never requests that reviewer.
/src/                                   @RevantCI @HANDLE-TBD

# User-facing documentation.
/docs/USER_MANUAL.md                    @RevantCI @HANDLE-TBD
/README.md                              @RevantCI @HANDLE-TBD
